---
title: Inline text decorations
---

# Inline text decorations {% #top %}

This document exercises every inline decoration the renderer applies to a
run of text: weight, slant, strikethrough, inline code, links, and colour.
Render it with `decorations.style.toml` so the link underline shows.

## One at a time

- **Bold** — from `**bold**`
- _Italic_ — from `_italic_`
- ~~Strikethrough~~ — from `~~struck~~`, drawn as a rule through the text
- `inline code` — from backticks, set in a monospace font
- [A hyperlink](https://example.com) — tinted, and underlined by this style
- {% color value="#c026d3" %}Coloured text{% /color %} — from `\{% color value="#c026d3" %}…\{% /color %}` (a `\{%` escapes a literal tag)

## Mid-paragraph

A single sentence can turn a run **bold**, _italic_, ~~struck through~~,
into `inline_code()`, a [hyperlink](https://example.com/docs), or
{% color value="#0891b2" %}a custom colour{% /color %} — each decoration
applies to just its own span while the prose flows around it.

## Combining them

Decorations nest, so a phrase can be **_bold and italic_** at once, a
{% color value="#dc2626" %}**bold red caution**{% /color %}, or a
deprecated call shown as ~~`legacy_api()`~~ — monospace with a strike
through it.

## Links

Every `[text](url)` link takes the document's `[link]` style. An external
target like [the docs](https://example.com/docs) opens in a browser; an
in-document jump such as [back to the top](#top) resolves to a page
destination. Both are underlined here.
